#: views/documentation.php:211
msgid "Current limitation:"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:211
msgid "This plugin currently supports single-site WordPress installations only. Multisite and network activation are not yet supported."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:212
msgid "Database:"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:212
msgid "Use MySQL 8.0 or newer or MariaDB 10.11 or newer with InnoDB available. MySQL 8.4 LTS is recommended for production. SQLite, PostgreSQL and unverified database-translation drop-ins are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:213
msgid "If an active site moves outside that database envelope, Booster leaves its stored data unchanged and pauses package storage, Transporter and deployments. Restore a supported database, then use read-only Troubleshooting to confirm compatibility. For planned moves, keep the normal site backup and a current Transporter Blueprint; Booster does not convert custom tables between database engines."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:214
msgid "PHP:"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:214
msgid "PHP 8.2 or newer is required, 8.4 LTS or newer recommended."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:221
msgid "Move managed packages without copying a development checkout"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:222
msgid "A Transporter Blueprint is a ZIP file that records the Booster-managed packages you select on this site and where their repos live. It is not a copy of the plugin or theme files installed here. The site that opens the Blueprint downloads its files from the committed repository, so local uncommitted changes, and local-only"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:222
msgid "folders, and other ignored and uncommitted dependencies are never included."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:223
msgid "Before a database or environment move"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:225
msgid "Export a current Transporter Blueprint containing every managed package."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:226
msgid "Optionally include the selected packages’ file-stored repository credentials in the password-protected archive."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:227
msgid "Preview the ZIP successfully and retain a copy off-site."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:228
msgid "Keep the normal database and filesystem backup."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:230
msgid "Complete database copies inside the supported MySQL or MariaDB and InnoDB envelope are best effort. A Transporter Blueprint is the supported reconstruction route when the copied Booster tables cannot be trusted, but the target database must still satisfy Booster’s requirements. Booster does not convert custom tables between database engines."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:231
msgid "Deployment attempts and delivery-replay history, webhook secrets and hooks registered with the Git provider, constants, locks and worker state, and source deployment policy remain target-local. Every installed or adopted package starts with deployment Disabled, so an administrator must deliberately choose a new target policy."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:232
msgid "Transporter workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:232
msgid "Select packages for a Transporter Blueprint on this site, open it on the other site, review what would change for each package, then apply only the selected changes. Excluded and unchecked packages remain untouched. Reviewing a Transporter Blueprint never installs anything, changes package settings, or stores the uploaded file — nothing happens until you apply it."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:233
msgid "Open Transporter"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:235
msgid "Step-by-step: moving a package to another site"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:237
msgid "Commit and push the exact branch, tag or commit you want the other site to install. A Transporter Blueprint never includes uncommitted local changes."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:238
msgid "If you are actively editing a package’s files on this site, set it to Disabled first so the Transporter Blueprint does not propose replacing files you are working on. Use Manual only when you want administrators on the other site to be able to update it through Booster."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:239
msgid "Choose which managed plugins and themes to include, then create a Transporter Blueprint. Credential transfer applies only to those selected packages and only when their credential is stored as a file rather than, for example, a constant. A package-only ZIP is unencrypted; including credentials requires a password and AES-256 encryption."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:240
msgid "On the other site, upload the ZIP, enter its password if you set one, then select Review Transporter Blueprint. Booster shows which packages it can install or adopt and which are already managed, protected, or blocked. An already-managed row can import its verified Blueprint credential without changing package settings; select only the actions you want Booster to apply."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:241
msgid "Apply only the changes you choose. Booster re-reads the ZIP and re-checks each package and repository right before applying it, so if something changed since your review, that one change is skipped safely and the others continue."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:242
msgid "On the other site, confirm repository access works and the package behaves as expected. Set up Push-to-Deploy separately, and only once that site is ready to receive automatic deployments."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:250
msgid "Move retained WP Pusher packages into Booster"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:251
msgid "If this site used WP Pusher 3.0.13, the temporary RAN Booster WP Pusher Migrator can adopt supported installed plugins and themes into Booster without reinstalling them. Each adopted package starts with deployment Disabled."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:253
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:255
msgid "Back up the site and deactivate WP Pusher. Booster and WP Pusher must not control package changes at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:256
msgid "Install and activate the migrator from its verified release package."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:257
msgid "For private repositories, add the replacement repository credential to Booster first. WP Pusher credentials are not copied."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:260
msgid "Migration workflow"
