#: views/documentation.php:476
msgid "Where this came from"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:477
msgid "Booster is a developer-focused repository deployment plugin for WordPress. It began as a modified derivative of WP Pusher 3.0.13. WP Pusher was created by Peter Suhm, and the inherited source was distributed under GPLv2. We are grateful for Peter’s original work and its central idea: use WordPress’s updater to deploy plugins and themes from version-controlled repositories."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:478
msgid "WP Pusher changed ownership in 2021 and is a separate product. Booster is an independent fork maintained by Rockets Are Nostalgic. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Peter Suhm, WP Pusher or its owners. The distributed NOTICE.md and license.txt record the full source provenance and license."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:480
msgid "Why we built this"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:481
msgid "The inherited release depended on a vendor-hosted licensing, OAuth and repository-picker service just to work at all — repository access, credential storage and even the repository browser all ran through that service. We forked it to remove that dependency. Every credential, webhook and deployment decision now lives on your own site, not a third party’s."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:483
msgid "What’s different"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:485
msgid "Safety."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:485
msgid "Booster verifies a repository’s identity and an archive’s contents before it touches a file, and will not let a delayed or out-of-order webhook roll back code that has already been updated. Saved credentials use authenticated encryption in a file with restrictive"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:485
msgid "permissions; the independent key remains in the WordPress database, so neither a file-only nor database-only copy contains usable credentials."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:486
msgid "Transporter."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:486
msgid "A password-protected Transporter Blueprint moves package and repository configuration, and any credentials you choose, between sites without copying a development checkout."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:487
msgid "Independence & Security."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:487
msgid "No vendor-hosted licensing, OAuth broker or repository-picker service. Further, the inherited codebase stored a private repository’s access token as a WordPress option in the database; Booster instead saves your repository credential in a file on your own site, never in the WordPress database."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:488
msgid "Extensibility."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:488
msgid "Additional git providers can be added through a documented registration hook without modifying Booster itself."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:491
msgid "How a deployment stays honest"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:492
msgid "Every deployment is recorded as one attempt with a clear status —"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:492
msgid "— so there is always an honest history and something concrete to point to if something goes wrong. Beyond that record, Booster protects a deployment in a few concrete ways:"
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:494
msgid "It will not deploy an old version over a newer one."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:494
msgid "If a webhook arrives late or out of order, Booster checks the repository’s current commit before replacing anything, so a delayed notification cannot roll back code that has already been updated."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:495
msgid "It verifies the download before touching any files."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:495
msgid "Before installing anything, Booster checks the downloaded archive’s exact contents, confirms it matches the expected package, and confirms every file it contains stays inside the expected folder."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:496
msgid "WordPress Core does the actual file replacement."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:496
msgid "Booster hands the verified files to WordPress’s own updater, which owns backup behaviour during the swap. Booster then checks the result and will show you a warning rather than reporting success when the outcome is unclear."
msgstr ""

#: views/documentation.php:498
msgid "Booster delegates package replacement to WordPress Core. It does not build, test or make untrusted repository code safe."
msgstr ""

